+# What a workout is
+
+The methodology the planner judges against. A human writes it (TRAINER.md); the engine never holds it and the validator never checks it (ADR-0001). Every line is a criterion for the planner's judgement, not a rule: where the planner has a reason to go another way, it goes, and says why in the block's `reason`.
+
+**Draft.** Written for the user to edit. The sources are cited from memory and have not been checked against the papers.
+
+Vocabulary is CONTEXT.md's. A **set** is one round of one exercise.
+
+## A working set
+
+| | criterion | source |
+|---|---|---|
+| effort | ends 0-3 reps short of failure; a set that ends far from it does not count as one | [5] |
+| reps | anywhere from about 6 to 30 builds muscle if the effort holds; heavy low-rep work builds strength best | [3], [6] |
+| body weight and bands | the load is fixed, so the **variant** sets the effort: pick the one whose failure lands inside the rep target, and progress by making it harder, not by adding reps without end | [3], [7] |
+| warm-up sets | not working sets; they cost time and count for nothing here | |
+
+## How much a group gets
+
+| | criterion | source |
+|---|---|---|
+| per muscle, per cycle | at least 10 working sets; fewer still works, more works better up to a point nobody has pinned down | [1] |
+| per group, per workout | about 4-10 working sets, more when the group appears once in the cycle and fewer when it appears twice | [1], [2] |
+| exercises per group | 1-3. A second exercise is there for a different pattern, muscle or length, not for variety | [2] |
+| sets per exercise | 2-4. Add a set before adding an exercise | [2] |
+| variants of one movement | four push-up variants are one movement four times; the second variant earns its place only if it shifts the work (incline vs decline, wide vs close) | |
+
+## Rest by intent
+
+The bands in `PLANNING` stand. The reason for them:
+
+| intent | rest | why | source |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| heavy compound, strength | 2-3 min | short rest costs reps on the next set, and reps are the stimulus | [4] |
+| compound, hypertrophy | 90-120 s | long enough that the next set is still a working set | [4], [8] |
+| isolation, small muscle | 60-90 s | the muscle recovers faster and the whole body is barely taxed | [8] |
+| between paired exercises | 0-30 s | the partner set is the other muscle's rest | [9] |
+
+Shorter rest is not free time: it buys minutes by lowering the quality of every set after the first.
+
+## Which structure
+
+| structure | reach for it when | avoid it when | source |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| **straight sets** | the main movement of a group, heavy or hard work, the first block of the workout | | [8] |
+| **superset**, antagonists or unrelated groups | time is short and the two do not compete: push with pull, biceps with triceps, chest with core. Saves about half the rest with no loss of reps | | [8], [9] |
+| **superset**, same muscle | finishing a group already worked, on purpose | it is the main work: the second exercise starts tired | [8] |
+| **circuit** | conditioning is the goal, or the time is so short that a full-body circuit is the only way to touch every group | it is how the plan fits the clock. Five exercises for one muscle in a circuit are five sets done tired, not five exercises | [8] |
+
+**The test for a circuit or a superset**: would the same exercises as straight sets be the better workout if the time allowed? If yes, and the time does allow, use straight sets.
+
+## Spending the time
+
+- **The time is spent on working sets, not on exercises.** With time left, add a set to an exercise already in the plan before adding a new one.
+- **Main work first**: the hardest movement for each group while fresh, isolation after.
+- **Every group asked for gets its main work before any group gets extra.**
+
+## An example
+
+Chest and arms, 45 minutes, body weight and bands. A shape, not an answer; the minutes are the engine's to compute.
+
+| block | exercises | rounds | rest | why |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | push-up, the variant that fails at 8-12 | 4 | 2 min | main chest work, fresh |
+| 2 | band chest fly + band curl | 3 | 90 s | second chest angle, paired with an arm muscle that does not compete |
+| 3 | bench dip | 3 | 90 s | main triceps work |
+| 4 | band overhead triceps extension + band hammer curl | 3 | 60 s | the long head of the triceps, and the forearm side of the biceps |
+
+Seven exercises, not nine; chest 7 sets, triceps 6, biceps 6. The session-7 plan had four push-up variants for 12 sets of one movement.
+
+## Not here
+
+- What is admissible, what fits, what repeats: the engine's.
+- Progression and return from a break: after 1.0.0 (ROADMAP).
+- The goal: chosen at onboarding (TRAINER.md). This draft assumes **muscle and strength together**; a goal of conditioning or of pure strength changes the rest and structure tables first.
+
